title: 'sp-database: aggregate same-key refcount ops within a transaction'
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: "Fix a kvdb refcount-leak: multiple `Store`/`Reference`/`Release` ops\
    \ on the same key in one `sp_database::Transaction` each read a stale on-disk\
    \ counter and write back to the same counter key \u2014 the underlying `DBTransaction`\
    \ keeps only the last `put`, collapsing N ops to a single \xB11. `commit_impl`\
    \ now aggregates per-`(col, key)` deltas first and performs one read-modify-write\
    \ per unique key.\n\nSurfaces when multiple displaced fork branches at the same\
    \ height carry the same indexed extrinsics. `prune_displaced_branches` then issues\
    \ `release(col11, hash) \xD7 N` per fork **in one finalization commit** \u2014\
    \ pre-fix only one decrement landed, leaving indexed transaction data reachable\
    \ past its retention period.\n\nAdds parametrized tests across `KvdbMemdb` / `ParityDb`\
    \ / `RocksDb` covering same-commit `Store + 2\xD7 Release`, `Store + 2\xD7 Reference`,\
    \ and `Store + Release` net-zero patterns. All three failed on the kvdb backends\
    \ pre-fix; all pass post-fix."
crates:
- name: sc-client-db
  bump: patch
- name: sp-database
  bump: patch
